Rule 1 now fires on:
- any Skip-family property (\bSkip\w*\s*=);
- any Trait or TraitAttribute;
- any attribute after [ or , other than the stock Fact/Theory that ends in Fact or Theory;
- a class deriving FactAttribute/TheoryAttribute.
The corpus test judges each row against rule 1 together with CountingRuleTestsAreNeverSkipped. 9 rows read before=quiet/now=fire; S20 is the bug test's own [WindowsTempFact]. Members no line pattern sees (non-public class, deleted [Fact], a foreign attribute, a by-name filter clause in the csproj) are closed by TheWindowsFolderFactsRunInTheDefaultSuite. With the custom-attribute pattern made inert, S20-S23 fail.
